22::
1:
Enable chain open\n
\n
\t\n

2:
Emergency stop\n
\n
\t\n

3:
Limit stop\n
\n
\t\n

6:
Auto stop\n
\n
\t\n

7:
Manual stop\n
\n
\t\n

8:
General stop\n
\n
\t\n

9:
Run chain status fault\n
Two channel status conflict.\n
\t\n
Check the leds on the system board\n
when the red ERR led is lit to see\n
where the fault is situated.
20:
Run chain status timeout\n
Two channel status timeout.\n
\n
The acknowledgement for a two channel\n
run chain status change was not\n
received within the expected time.\n
\t\n
Check the leds on the system board\n
when the red ERR led is lit to locate\n
the fault. You might have to order\n
Motors On to get the ERR led lit.\n
Check temp. switch in main transformer.
21:
Key speed status fault\n
The operating mode selector signals\n
and the speed signal are in conflict.\n
\t\n

22:
Key status fault\n
The operating mode selector signals\n
are in conflict (i.e. several modes or\n
no mode indicated).\n
\t\n

25:
Stop order timeout\n
The stop order was carried out\n
as a forced guard stop when\n
no acknowledgement was received\n
within the expected time\n
\t\n

26:
Run control status fault\n
Status conflict\n
between runchain relays and\n
run control.\n
\t\n
Replace system board
40:
Hold stop\n
\n
\t\n

41:
Motor 1-6 overload\n
One or several Motors are overheated.\n
Make sure to let the Motors cool down\n
before ordering Motors On again.\n
This error will otherwise occur again\n
after 15 sec in Motors On state.\n
\t\n
View Safety in the IO window and wait\n
until the signal OLM1 equals 0 before\n
ordering Motors On again.
42:
Motor 7-x overload\n
One or several Motors are overheated.\n
Make sure to let the Motors cool down\n
before ordering Motors On again.\n
This error will otherwise occur again\n
after 15 sec in Motors On state.\n
\t\n
View Safety in the IO window and wait\n
until the signal OLM7 equals 0 before\n
ordering Motors On again.
